  "section_notes": "S1 imposes very strict reporting (24h for all incidents, 48h customer notice) with broad scope. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% threshold but explicitly does not prohibit sale above it, while requiring per-model numeric results to customers and not public publication. S3 requires 6-year retrofit, S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months with possible equivalent, and S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notices and no transition."
